{"kind":"stack","id":"digest-s1","title":"The digestive system: quiz, flash cards and a story","theme":{"background":"#fdf6e3","foreground":"#073642","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","id":"c1-p","picto":"apple"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-q","content":"Where does digestion of food begin?"},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a","label":"In the mouth","why":"Chewing and saliva start breaking food down in the mouth.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"In the stomach","why":"Pupils may think the stomach is the first organ, but it comes later.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-c","label":"In the large intestine","why":"Pupils may think the end of the tract is where digestion starts.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Mouth"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"Teeth chew food into small pieces, and saliva starts to break it down."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"What is the main job of the stomach?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"To break food down with strong acid and churning","why":"The stomach churns food and uses acid to break it down further.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"To absorb most of the water from food","why":"Pupils may confuse the stomach with the large intestine, which absorbs water.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"To make bile","why":"Pupils may mix up the stomach with the liver, which makes bile.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-t","content":"You have eaten a big lunch. Your stomach feels full. What do you do?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Go for a gentle walk","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Lie down straight away","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"The walk helps food move on through your gut. Your body digests well."},{"type":"button","id":"c5-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"Lying down can make the stomach acid rise. It feels uncomfortable, but it passes."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-q","content":"Which organ absorbs most of the nutrients from digested food?"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-a","label":"The small intestine","why":"Its long, folded lining takes in most nutrients into the blood.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"The stomach","why":"Pupils may think the stomach absorbs food, but it mainly breaks it down.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-c","label":"The large intestine","why":"Pupils may think it absorbs nutrients, but it mainly takes water.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"Large intestine"},{"type":"text","id":"c8-e","content":"It absorbs water from undigested food and stores the waste until it leaves the body."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"What does the liver do in digestion?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"It makes bile to help break down fats","why":"Bile is made in the liver and helps digest fats in the small intestine.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"It stores the food we swallow","why":"Pupils may think storage happens in the liver, but food is stored in the stomach.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"It chews food into small pieces","why":"Pupils may think the liver does the chewing, but teeth do that in the mouth.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which part of the digestive system is the food tube that links the mouth and stomach?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"The oesophagus","why":"The oesophagus is the tube that carries food from the mouth to the stomach.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"The trachea","why":"Pupils may mix up the food tube with the windpipe, which carries air.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"The rectum","why":"Pupils may think of the rectum as the start of the tube, but it is near the end.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done on the digestive system!"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"You now know how each main part helps turn food into energy for your body."}],"actions":[]}}
